{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#913","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#913","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#913\",\"parent_revision\":\"18d141ae35399466d8352e1e77d0e0f68301d3da\",\"root_revision\":\"1e41862ba40cba46d1fe7d4d8df98ab42897010ca71220ce736ecd6fe9302152\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nTwo issues in the new discover_repo() function in backlog_core/models.py: (1) DEFAULT_REPO = discover_repo() executes at module import time, triggering a subprocess call on every import. Should be lazy \u2014 use GitPython for import-time safety or make DEFAULT_REPO a lazy property. (2) ssh://git@github.com/owner/repo.git URL format is not matched by either _SSH_REMOTE_RE or _HTTPS_REMOTE_RE regex. This silently falls through to RepoDiscoveryError for users with ssh:// protocol remotes.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **fix discover_repo() import-time execution and ssh:// url parsing** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Code review and user observation 2026-03-20 during #852 implementation\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-20\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"4579e5ea9f5659d595e858eae02bd8d5340963f62ef35ea5bde76e674b1059cb\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABXN5PeQ\"}"}